Z||000000||jhogans||12-21-1999||09:52 PM||||Are there any shift gates out there for the Fiero.  I've seen them on European cars and was curious if there are some for the Fiero.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||12-21-1999||09:58 PM||||I've always wondered if there are any kits like that around anymore.<BR>Go here for a picture: <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/euroshifter.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/euroshifter.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||jhogans||12-21-1999||10:01 PM||||That's what I'm talking about.  Who sells them?  It looks like Rodney sells the replacement shifters||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||12-21-1999||11:05 PM||||I have one of the FiEuro gate shifters. It doesn't actually shift into the gates. More or less there is a big space between the gates and the shifter doesn't even come close to the actual gates, but just shifts in the middle part. I removed mine because of this. It still looks brand new. <P>The stick is long and has a huge ball on the end. The gate bolts down to the plastic panel and there is a piece of fabric that has a rubber grommit in the center. The stick goes through this to hide all the stuff underneath. My wife (was my girlfriend at the time) bought it for me for my birthday way back in 92 (I think 92). A long time ago. The people that sold it are out of business I think. I will try to locate the invoice and get the info fer ya.||||reg||3
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||12-21-1999||11:10 PM||||I can't believe I found it!! Seems she bought it for me on 12/06/93. Cost was $79.95 (U.S.) $3.00 shipping<P>Performancs Products INC.<BR>9 Jeanette Drive<BR>Plainville, CT. 06062||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||12:44 AM||||Why would you want a gated shifter that doesn't shift into the gates?  Just wondering. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||jhogans||12-22-1999||01:47 AM||||That sucks that it doesn't shift into the gates.||||reg||5
Z||000007||four50four||12-22-1999||12:32 PM||||me being an idiot and all, what exactly is a gate??||||reg||4
Z||000008||fiero56||12-22-1999||01:10 PM||||The gates are the open spaces between the "fingers". The way most gated shifters work, is the stick slides in between the fingers, looks real cool. Aparently the FiEuro shifter doesn't even reach the fingers. Just jumps around in the middle.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-22-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||william_thorniii||12-22-1999||05:25 PM||||Hey guys.... Why do you want gated shifters?  If you just want them for the European look that is respectable.  The real issue lies in the fact that they make shifting a Fiero much more difficult.  People always complain about our current shifting being "notchy"... a gated shifter is much more so.  I think that the aforementioned shifter is a good idea.  You meet in the middle... it looks like a gated shifter, but you don't have to put up with the awful shifting that is associated with one.  Of course this is all my opinion.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
